MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "Step Back and Different Shades Of Blue felt like natural next listens because their blues guitar connects closely with what drew me to Old Sock and People, Hell & Angels.",
    "High Hopes, Before This World, and Old Yellow Moon also touched on my interest in rock, singer-songwriters, and roots music, even though blues guitar was my priority today."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "25's pop ballads, Morning Phase's subdued mood, and Wallflower's jazz-oriented interpretations did not offer the guitar-driven sound I wanted on this visit.",
    "Nothing Has Changed offered a career-spanning collection when I was more interested in exploring another blues-rock album; familiarity alone did not make it a compelling choice."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "The choices seemed to treat a broad connection to familiar rock and singer-songwriter music as enough, although those sounds serve different listening moods for me.",
    "Recognizable albums seemed to receive too much emphasis compared with whether their guitar work and blues feel matched what I wanted today."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "My Clapton and Hendrix listening points toward expressive blues guitar, which mattered more today than a general connection to rock.",
    "An album can interest me without prompting a choice now: I rarely select many things, and the two strongest guitar-focused matches were enough."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my broad musical interests but only partly captured my current preference for guitar-led blues over other familiar sounds."
}
